  "body_html": "<h1>Strategy In A Perfect-Information Game</h1>\n<p>For a player $i$, a pure strategy is a function on $P_i$ that assigns to each\nposition $p\\in P_i$ a successor in $S(p)$. Thus a strategy specifies what the\nplayer would do at every position where that player might move, including\npositions that are not reached by the realized play.</p>",
